'' '__FB_QUERY_SYMBOL__( query, symbol )' -- fbc's compile-time symbol query. Every
'' answer here was MEASURED against fbc over the same twenty-six symbols, and four of
'' them do not follow from the names in fbc-int/symbol.bi:
''
''   a PARAMETER reads as FB_SYMBCLASS_VAR, not _PARAM
''   an ENUM MEMBER reads as FB_SYMBCLASS_CONST, and its datatype is _ENUM
''   'type C extends object' is _STRUCT, not _CLASS
''   'zstring * 8' is CHAR and 'string * 8' is FIXSTR -- not the same answer
''
'' The datatype is ENCODED -- base type in the low five bits, pointer level in the next
'' four, one const bit per level from bit 9 -- so 'const zstring ptr' is 1060 and
'' 'long ptr ptr' is 75.
''
'' The query codes are only ever written as ENUM MEMBERS three levels deep
'' ('fbc.FB_QUERY_SYMBOL.symbclass'), and an enum member named through its enum was
'' bound to nothing at all: 'dim as long a = E.elem' allocated a and stored nothing.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: --dump-ir tests/mir/src/query-symbol.bas
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-OUT: verify: ok
'' EXPECT-OUT: 0 statements not lowered
'' GOLDEN: expected/query-symbol.out
